  Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 §4(b)) — this file has been modified from
  the original:

    - Standardization parameters (per-feature means and standard deviations)
      learned during `fit` are stored on the model and re-applied at
      `transform` time, so new data lands in the same coordinate space as the
      training scores. The original standardized only at fit.
    - Fitting is seedable: the random initialisation of the loading matrix
      takes an explicit seed, making a fit reproducible run to run.
    - Model persistence round-trips the full parameter set (loadings, means,
      standard deviations, eigenvalues) rather than the loadings alone.

    - The inherited approximate missing-data loop is replaced by direct
      observed-data Gaussian likelihood optimisation using L-BFGS-B, with
      multiple starts and explicit gradient-convergence checks. Missing
      entries are completed with fitted Gaussian conditional means.
    - Complete data use the analytic PPCA maximum-likelihood solution.
      Saved state includes Gaussian loadings, residual variance and fit
      diagnostics, separately from the orthonormal projection axes.

  The Gaussian model follows Tipping, M. E. and Bishop, C. M. (1999),
  "Probabilistic Principal Component Analysis", Journal of the Royal
  Statistical Society, Series B, 61(3), 611-622. The current incomplete-data
  optimiser is direct likelihood optimisation, not the inherited EM loop.

